WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:03.036
-I'm gonna make a couple of
calls so I can see you play

00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:04.136
with some guys
on your level tomorrow.

00:00:04.136 --> 00:00:06.972
-I gotta work.
-How old are you?

00:00:06.972 --> 00:00:08.341
-22.

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:10.576
-Basketball years
are like dog years.

00:00:10.576 --> 00:00:14.047
If we're gonna do this,
we actually gotta do this now.

00:00:14.047 --> 00:00:17.316
-And...how much money
will you pay him?

00:00:17.316 --> 00:00:18.351
-To come to Philly?

00:00:18.351 --> 00:00:21.153
It'll be
a pro-rated league minimum.

00:00:21.153 --> 00:00:24.423
-But you say he was great, for
great, you pay the maximum, no?

00:00:24.423 --> 00:00:25.925
-[ Chuckles ] Yeah, yes.

00:00:25.925 --> 00:00:30.030
NBA contract
of any kind is maximum, no?

00:00:31.631 --> 00:00:33.633
-And how much is the minimum?

00:00:33.633 --> 00:00:38.203
-Minimum salary in the NBA
is $900,000.

00:00:38.203 --> 00:00:39.872
-He will call in sick.

00:00:39.872 --> 00:00:42.475
-Welcome back to "Late Night."
We're here with Adam Sandler.

00:00:42.475 --> 00:00:45.177
That was a clip from his new
film, "Hustle," which is great.

00:00:45.177 --> 00:00:48.681
-Thank you, man.
-And this is...

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:50.583
this script came via

00:00:50.583 --> 00:00:52.085
Lebron James'
production company.

00:00:52.085 --> 00:00:54.054
-Yes, yes.
-Him and Maverick Carter,

00:00:54.054 --> 00:00:56.188
they're wonderful guys.
-Great guys,

00:00:56.188 --> 00:00:58.124
and they have a movie business,

00:00:58.124 --> 00:00:59.325
and they had this great script

00:00:59.325 --> 00:01:03.195
about a scout
that discovers a guy overseas,

00:01:03.195 --> 00:01:05.431
and he tries
to get him in the NBA.

00:01:05.431 --> 00:01:07.100
It really was amazing.

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:08.668
So I read the script,
and I was like,

00:01:08.668 --> 00:01:11.104
"This is awesome, and thank you
so much for thinking of me."

00:01:11.104 --> 00:01:13.473
And I called the guys up,
and I said, "I loved it,

00:01:13.473 --> 00:01:16.241
I loved the character,
and I loved the fact that,

00:01:16.241 --> 00:01:17.410
you know, he was a scout.

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:19.813
He's smart,
he weighs 220 pounds."

00:01:19.813 --> 00:01:23.016
And they were like, "What do
you mean with the 220 pounds?"

00:01:23.016 --> 00:01:24.116
And I go, "Well,
it said it in the script

00:01:24.116 --> 00:01:25.318
he weighs 250, right?"

00:01:25.318 --> 00:01:27.519
And they go,
"You just said 220."

00:01:27.519 --> 00:01:29.556
I go, "He weighs 280 pounds..."

00:01:29.556 --> 00:01:31.457
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.457 --> 00:01:32.825
"...and I'd love to do it."

00:01:32.825 --> 00:01:34.526
And they were like,
"Do you weigh that now?"

00:01:34.526 --> 00:01:37.363
I said, "No, I'm 160,
but I can get there in a day."

00:01:37.363 --> 00:01:39.598
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.598 --> 00:01:42.802
-Incredible cast, I mean,
you're a natural in it.

00:01:42.802 --> 00:01:45.070
Juancho,
who's an actual NBA player,

00:01:45.070 --> 00:01:48.107
is a fantastic actor in this.
-Unbelievable. I know.

00:01:48.107 --> 00:01:51.010
-Does it drive you crazy when
an athlete's also a good actor?

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:52.478
-All these guys in the movie,

00:01:52.478 --> 00:01:54.414
all the NBA guys,
they're just cool.

00:01:54.414 --> 00:01:56.182
They're cool, they're confident.

00:01:56.182 --> 00:01:58.818
They probably,
their entire life,

00:01:58.818 --> 00:02:00.186
have been told they're cool.

00:02:00.186 --> 00:02:02.455
They're just better
at everything.

00:02:04.924 --> 00:02:06.392
Juancho's just handsome as hell.

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:09.328
He's 6'9", there's
no room he doesn't walk into

00:02:09.328 --> 00:02:11.264
that everybody doesn't go,
"Hey, look at that guy."

00:02:11.264 --> 00:02:13.132
So, I don't know, he just --

00:02:13.132 --> 00:02:15.435
but he was such a great guy,
such a great actor.

00:02:15.435 --> 00:02:18.671
And I would tell him
after takes,

00:02:18.671 --> 00:02:19.905
'cause he would play it so real

00:02:19.905 --> 00:02:21.841
and look deep into my eyes
and say stuff,

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:23.576
and I was going,
"Geez, this guy's good."

00:02:23.576 --> 00:02:26.512
But I would tell him
how great he was,

00:02:26.512 --> 00:02:27.880
and he'd be like, "At what?"

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:29.982
I'd be like, "At that scene,
you were just great."

00:02:29.982 --> 00:02:30.883
He'd go, "oh, okay."

00:02:30.883 --> 00:02:32.217
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.217 --> 00:02:34.353
He didn't care. He didn't care.
It meant nothing to him.

00:02:34.353 --> 00:02:36.856
-I always thought athletes
were great at "SNL",

00:02:36.856 --> 00:02:38.758
because they would never
get nervous

00:02:38.758 --> 00:02:40.493
because it was so meaningless

00:02:40.493 --> 00:02:42.462
compared to what
they actually did for a living.

00:02:42.462 --> 00:02:44.931
-Ah, you're right, you're right.
-Like, no athlete

00:02:44.931 --> 00:02:47.367
could be so bad on "SNL"
they'd get cut from a team.

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:49.602
[ Laughter ]
-That's so funny.

00:02:49.602 --> 00:02:52.138
-"I'm one of the best players
in the world, this is stupid."

00:02:52.138 --> 00:02:54.474
-Who did you have?
You had Peyton Manning.

00:02:54.474 --> 00:02:56.509
-We had Peyton,
we had Brady, yeah.

00:02:56.509 --> 00:02:58.211
We had Barkley.
Did you have Barkley?

00:02:58.211 --> 00:03:00.513
-We had Barkley, too.
Great, funny guy.

00:03:00.513 --> 00:03:02.582
We had Barkley,
we had Michael Jordan.

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:04.350
When I was there,
Michael Jordan hosted.

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:05.685
He hung out with us.

00:03:05.685 --> 00:03:08.321
That was, like,
we were so in love with him.

00:03:08.321 --> 00:03:10.356
Everyone was in love with MJ

00:03:10.356 --> 00:03:12.525
'cause he was such a sweetheart
and so nice to us.

00:03:12.525 --> 00:03:14.760
And he would say your name.

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:16.695
Remember when a superstar
says your name,

00:03:16.695 --> 00:03:17.897
you're just like,
"He knows my name."

00:03:17.897 --> 00:03:19.799
And it's just incredible.
You know what's funny?

00:03:19.799 --> 00:03:22.168
I don't know if I ever told you
this -- Bruce Springsteen.

00:03:22.168 --> 00:03:25.338
I love Bruce Springsteen,
and so I was working out --

00:03:25.338 --> 00:03:28.208
I might've told this story,
but I'll tell it anyways

00:03:28.208 --> 00:03:29.809
and you can cut it out
if it's too long.

00:03:29.809 --> 00:03:35.548
So I went to a gym on, like,
60th Street in East Side.

00:03:35.548 --> 00:03:36.382
I used to work out.

00:03:36.382 --> 00:03:37.450
I used to go,

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:39.152
"I'm not as funny
as everybody on the show,

00:03:39.152 --> 00:03:40.186
but I'm gonna look better."

00:03:40.186 --> 00:03:41.487
[ Laughter ]

00:03:41.487 --> 00:03:44.056
Right, so anyways, I work out,
I go to this gym,

00:03:44.056 --> 00:03:46.225
and I'm working out
at this real crappy gym.

00:03:46.225 --> 00:03:47.293
I forget the name of it.

00:03:47.293 --> 00:03:49.862
But anyways,
I keep seeing this guy.

00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:52.097
I'm like, "That guy looks like
Bruce Springsteen."

00:03:52.097 --> 00:03:56.302
So I go, "Oh, this
can't be Bruce Springsteen."

00:03:56.302 --> 00:03:58.771
Anyway, I'm going,
"From that angle,

00:03:58.771 --> 00:03:59.772
it looks like Bruce Springsteen.

00:03:59.772 --> 00:04:01.707
We're working out
at the same gym.

00:04:01.707 --> 00:04:03.909
There're no way he'd be at this
crap gym," blah, blah, blah.

00:04:03.909 --> 00:04:06.946
Anyways, I know I'm talking
a lot, but here we go.

00:04:06.946 --> 00:04:10.349
So [laughs] anyways,

00:04:10.349 --> 00:04:13.051
Bruce Springsteen walks by,
I'm on the thing that --

00:04:13.051 --> 00:04:14.386
this one, I'm doing this.

00:04:14.386 --> 00:04:16.956
He stops right on me, I'm
looking right at Springsteen.

00:04:16.956 --> 00:04:18.825
I'm like, "That is
Bruce Springsteen."

00:04:18.825 --> 00:04:20.826
He goes, "Hey." I go, "Hey."

00:04:20.826 --> 00:04:23.962
And he goes, "I know you,"
and I go, "You do?"

00:04:23.962 --> 00:04:26.966
And he goes,
"You're, uh, Allan Stanley."

00:04:26.966 --> 00:04:30.136
[ Laughter ]
And I go, "Yeah, yeah, yeah."

00:04:30.136 --> 00:04:34.440
So, anyways, I come back
to the show,

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:37.043
and I see Farley,
I'm like, "Dude,

00:04:37.043 --> 00:04:39.845
I saw Bruce Springsteen
at the gym."

00:04:39.845 --> 00:04:43.516
He's like, "No you didn't."
I go, "He knew me! He knew me!"

00:04:43.516 --> 00:04:45.985
And he's like, "There no way
that's -- there's no way."

00:04:45.985 --> 00:04:49.088
I go, "He called me Allan
Stanley, but he knew me,

00:04:49.088 --> 00:04:51.023
he recognized me from the show,"
and blah, blah, blah.

00:04:51.023 --> 00:04:54.693
So anyways, and then everyone's
kind of, the next day,

00:04:54.693 --> 00:04:55.861
walking around, they're going,
they're saying, like,

00:04:55.861 --> 00:04:57.029
"You're lying."

00:04:57.029 --> 00:04:58.230
And I was like,
"It was Bruce Springsteen,

00:04:58.230 --> 00:04:59.865
he knew me,"
and blah, blah, blah.

00:04:59.865 --> 00:05:01.467
So, like, two years later,

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:04.704
Springsteen is the musical guest
on the show,

00:05:04.704 --> 00:05:06.439
and he's coming by

00:05:06.439 --> 00:05:08.341
and he's saying hi to everybody
and blah, blah, blah.

00:05:08.341 --> 00:05:10.109
And I'm standing there, I'm
like, "There's no way," right?

00:05:10.109 --> 00:05:12.611
Then he looks at me
and goes, "Hey, man,"

00:05:12.611 --> 00:05:13.913
and everyone
kind of looks and he goes,

00:05:13.913 --> 00:05:15.481
"You still go to that gym?"

00:05:15.481 --> 00:05:18.351
[ Laughter ]
And I was like, "That's right."

00:05:18.351 --> 00:05:21.520
[ Laughter ]

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:23.055
-Allan Stanley!
-Allan Stanley.

00:05:23.055 --> 00:05:24.456
-Keeping it tight.
-Yeah.

00:05:24.456 --> 00:05:26.926
-Hey, congratulations
on the film. It's fantastic.

00:05:26.926 --> 00:05:28.794
It is always the best
to have you here.

00:05:28.794 --> 00:05:30.762
You guys, Adam Sandler.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:30.762 --> 00:05:32.598
"Hustle" in select theaters now

00:05:32.598 --> 00:05:33.900
and available on Netflix
tomorrow.

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:35.735
We'll be right back
with James Patterson.

